---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StepsStrip from '../components/StepsStrip.astro';
import ConvertDoor from '../components/ConvertDoor.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Will the picture look better as a PNG?',
    a: 'No, and this page will not pretend otherwise. A JPG has already thrown detail away; writing its pixels into a PNG stores exactly what is there, nothing more. The picture does not improve; the file gets bigger, often much bigger. What improves is what happens next: the pixels stop changing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Then why convert at all?',
    a: 'Two honest reasons. Some portals, editors and print queues accept PNG and not JPG, and the door is the door. And every time a JPG is opened and saved again as a JPG, it loses a little more; a PNG freezes the picture as it is now, so further editing starts from a file that no longer degrades.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much bigger will it be?',
    a: 'Photos commonly land several times their JPG size as a PNG; the result line prints both sizes, so the trade is never silent. If the size is the problem, this is the wrong door: compress image lands a JPG on an exact KB target.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my file go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is decoded, re-encoded and offered back to you inside this page. Nothing is uploaded.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to convert a JPG to a PNG",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick a JPG", text: "Drop a JPG on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device. A file in the wrong format is pointed at the right door." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Convert to PNG", text: "Press 'Convert to PNG'. There is no quality setting: the JPG is decoded and its pixels are written into a PNG exactly, here in the page." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Download the PNG", text: "Download the PNG; the result line prints the bytes before and after, because the file grows and the picture does not change." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="JPG to PNG: convert a JPG to a PNG, free, in your browser · Benchzy" description="Convert one JPG to a PNG inside your browser: an exact, lossless copy of the picture as it is, for doors that require PNG and editing that should stop losing quality. The file grows; the picture does not change. No upload, no account.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">Image tools · convert</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">JPG to PNG</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Some doors only open for a PNG. This door converts one JPG to a PNG, here in your
        browser, and it is honest about the trade before you run: the PNG holds every pixel
        of your JPG exactly, the picture does not get better, and the file gets bigger.
        What you gain is a picture that stops degrading every time it is saved. A whole
        folder at once is the
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/batch-convert-images/">batch convert page</a>;
        the reverse trip is <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/png-to-jpg/">PNG to JPG</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <StepsStrip who="For one JPG that has to arrive as a PNG: a portal or editor that requires PNG, or a picture you are about to edit and re-save." steps={[{ n: '01', t: 'Pick a JPG' }, { n: '02', t: 'Convert to PNG' }, { n: '03', t: 'Download the PNG' }]} />

    <ConvertDoor from="jpeg" to="png" note="The wrapper changes, and the picture does not. Every pixel of your JPG is written into the PNG exactly as it decoded: nothing added, nothing sharpened. Expect the file to grow, often a lot; the result line prints both sizes." />

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The JPG is decoded by the open-source jSquash codecs and the decoded picture is
          written as a PNG, losslessly, the same engine the batch convert page runs. The
          first run loads the image program (about 2 MB, one time only). The download is how
          we protect your privacy: the program comes to your device and does the work there,
          so your file never leaves it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          PNG cannot put back what JPG already threw away: soft edges, blocky patches and
          lost detail in your JPG are stored faithfully, not repaired, and no tool here
          claims to restore them. If the file size is your problem, this door makes it
          worse; the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/compress-image/">exact-KB tool</a>
          is the one that lands a JPG on a size a door sets.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/convert-image.js';
  </script>
</Base>
